"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nA novel that unfolds from the first-person perspective of . The reader empathizes with the protagonist Michael until the last moment and sees the world through his eyes.  \nTherefore, it provides an even more shocking twist when the truth is revealed and causes confusion in judgment.  \nThe Murder of Roger Ackroyd has a similar development.  \n\nPersonally, among works featuring such an , I enjoyed reading 's Malice the most.  \n\nThis work is said to have been chosen by  herself as one of her most cherished works.  \nIn this work, there is no great detective or complex alibi puzzle; it only doggedly follows the twisted inner self of a human, the perfect crime he designed, and the process of his own destruction.  "